From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:38:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/28] database: fail closed on write-log retention stalls

Expose retained write-log payload weight, entry count, timestamp span, subscription progress lag, trim activity, live metric-owner state, and fatal worker failures with explicit current-state and reset semantics.

Coordinate multiple subscription managers through a monotone enforced minimum so stale observations, leapfrogging managers, and empty appends cannot regress or freeze retention progress. Serialize owner gauges and republish a remaining owner's state when another database is dropped.

Use fair worker selection to prevent subscription churn from starving write-log advancement. Propagate internal subscription and advancement errors to local-backend fatal preemption, and route unwind-profile worker panics through the same boundary; production release panics continue to abort directly.
